# Dev-time runtime state in the fixtures store.
#
# The fixtures backend (packages/site-template/fixtures/) doubles as the
# seed content for new dev installs AND the live datastore when running
# the portal locally. These collections are 100% runtime — they never
# belong as seed:
#   - api_key_lookup/        root-level lookup index
#   - api_audit/             write-audit log
#   - api_keys/              user-created API key metadata
#   - deploys/               deploy job state
#   - working_copies/        the editor's unsaved-draft buffer
#   - _tombstones_*          chain-read tombstones for branch overrides
#
# working_copies/ is runtime by definition: it's the per-doc draft buffer
# that commitWorkingCopy() drains into the canonical doc. A committed one
# would seed every new dev install with someone else's half-finished edit,
# and deploys ignore it anyway (saved content only).
#
# Content collections (pages/, partials/, collections/.../items/, etc.)
# can't be gitignored at the path level because seed content lives there
# too — clean up agent-generated test content by hand or via `git restore`.
#
# Bigger fix: separate dev-runtime entirely from seed (TYPEROLL_FIXTURES_DIR
# pointing at a gitignored sibling, seed copied in on first boot).
# Tracked under docs/dev-runtime-isolation.md (TODO).
packages/site-template/fixtures/api_key_lookup/
packages/site-template/fixtures/organizations/*/sites/*/api_audit/
packages/site-template/fixtures/organizations/*/sites/*/api_keys/
packages/site-template/fixtures/organizations/*/sites/*/deploys/
packages/site-template/fixtures/organizations/*/sites/*/versions/*/working_copies/
packages/site-template/fixtures/organizations/*/sites/*/versions/*/_tombstones_*/

# Scratch dir for screenshots, generated images, and any throwaway working
# files — humans AND agents put temporary artifacts here, never in the repo
# root or a package dir. Contents are ignored; the dir itself is kept (.gitkeep)
# so it always exists. See CLAUDE.md → "Scratch / temporary files".
temp/*
!temp/.gitkeep
